  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "💐 Flower Shop Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a florist, from Peony for Your Thoughts to Maison Pivoine."
    },
    "intro": "A good florist name says flowers at a glance and is easy to say over the phone: your own name for a local shop, a pun for a stall, or a French word for a premium studio. Opening a florist, a flower stall or a wedding flower studio? This **flower shop name generator** has florist business names in eight styles, from puns to French, ready to check before you paint the sign.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good flower shop names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Stem Cellar</strong>: a clever pun for a basement or market stall.</li><li><strong>Seas the Daisy Flower Co.</strong>: cheerful and seaside.</li><li><strong>Clover & Stem</strong>: cute and gentle.</li><li><strong>Second Chance Flowers</strong>: funny, and you know exactly who's buying.</li><li><strong>Ingram & Bramhall Florists</strong>: a classic name that sounds like an established family firm.</li><li><strong>Studio Bough</strong>: modern and short.</li><li><strong>Atelier Muguet</strong>: French for a workshop of lily of the valley.</li><li><strong>Poppies by Sarah</strong>: your name with a favourite flower.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How florists name themselves",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Your own name</strong> builds trust for weddings and funerals, where people want to know who they're dealing with.</li><li><strong>A flower in the name</strong> tells people what you do: Peony, Posy, Larkspur, Clover.</li><li><strong>French</strong> suggests premium floristry: <em>fleur</em> is flower, <em>pivoine</em> peony, <em>muguet</em> lily of the valley and <em>lilas</em> lilac.</li><li><strong>The Victorians</strong> gave flowers meanings, known as floriography or the language of flowers, so a name can carry a message: forget-me-nots for remembrance, for example.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
        "content": "<p>Before you pay for a logo, labels or a stall banner, press <strong>Check</strong> on the name you like, or paste it into the <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a>. It looks for:</p><ul><li><strong>Company names:</strong> in the UK, Companies House won't register a limited company name that's the same as one already on the register. In the US, check your state's business register.</li><li><strong>Trade marks:</strong> search the UK Intellectual Property Office and, if you sell abroad, the USPTO. A registered company name doesn't give you trade mark rights.</li><li><strong>Web and social:</strong> the .com or .co.uk, plus the Instagram, TikTok and Etsy handles florist customers will look for.</li></ul><p>Many flower orders come through relay networks and online directories, so also check your name isn't close to one of the big flower brands customers might confuse you with.</p><p>This is general guidance, not legal advice. For the full checklist, read <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Tips for a florist",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Say it on the phone.</strong> If you have to spell it every time, simplify it.</li><li><strong>Think about weddings.</strong> A pun can feel too light for wedding and funeral flowers; a name or a French word suits them better.</li><li><strong>Make it work on a van and a ribbon,</strong> where it'll be seen most.</li></ul><p>Selling plants too? Try the <a href=\"plant-shop-name-generator.html\">Plant Shop Name Generator</a>. For a whole wedding business, there's the <a href=\"wedding-planner-name-generator.html\">Wedding Planner Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For more, see all the <a href=\"../categories/biz_shops-names.html\">shop and brand business name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
